    "text": "If<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mole</mi></math> of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> decompose at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bar</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the work is done (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math>) by one mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> as it expands against <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bar</mi></math> pressure is:<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8652;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.3</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>",
